.nf
YASMV manual                                                 scenario

.ti 0
SYNOPSIS

.in 3
scenario configure "<file>"
scenario list
scenario show [<id>]
scenario export [-o "<file>"]
scenario replay <implementation> [<id>]

.ti 0
DESCRIPTION

.fi
.in 3
Configure, export, inspect, and replay executable scenarios in the current
workspace. Quote IDs that are not native identifiers. Omitting an ID uses the
last selected scenario.

configure saves adapter mappings from a JSON file in a new model revision.
export replays the current native trace and saves a scenario using those
mappings. -o also writes it to a file, replacing existing contents.

list shows stored scenarios. show displays a complete scenario. replay runs
it against an implementation and reports a match or the first divergence.
The supported implementations are faulty and deduplicating for the retry
protocol adapter. Configure, export, and replay require a loaded model.

.ti 0
EXAMPLES

.nf
.in 3
>> scenario configure "examples/retry-protocol/scenario.json"
>> scenario export -o "/tmp/retry-scenario.json"
>> scenario replay faulty

.ti 0
SEE ALSO

.fi
.in 3
help workspace, help reach, help select-trace, help dump-trace, help job.
